WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.320
An unclear word tells you there is a speech sound problem.

2
00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:05.000
It does not tell you why.

3
00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:08.800
In a functional speech sound disorder, no physical cause is known.

4
00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:12.840
Childhood apraxia of speech is an organic motor planning disorder.

5
00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:15.240
The distinction matters because the assessment and

6
00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:18.080
intervention must fit the underlying problem.

7
00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:21.140
Compare repeated productions of the same word.

8
00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:23.840
In this teaching example, a predictable phonological

9
00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:27.800
pattern changes cat to tat each time.

10
00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:32.060
For the second profile, the same target changes across attempts.

11
00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:34.900
Inconsistent errors raise concern for apraxia, but

12
00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:38.440
inconsistency alone does not establish the diagnosis.

13
00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:40.300
Now watch how sounds join.

14
00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:43.000
Speech is a coordinated movement sequence.

15
00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:48.140
In apraxia, transitions between sounds or syllables may be lengthened or disrupted.

16
00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:51.440
Difficulty can increase as a word becomes longer or more complex.

17
00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:56.480
A wrong sound and a disrupted transition describe different observations.

18
00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:57.860
Record both.

19
00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:00.300
Listen for the rhythm of the word or phrase.

20
00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:02.160
Prosody includes stress.

21
00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:06.660
Inappropriate lexical or phrasal stress is the third consensus feature.

22
00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:09.940
Use the three together: inconsistent errors, lengthened

23
00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:14.300
or disrupted coarticulatory transitions, and inappropriate prosody.

24
00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:16.400
Make the decision from the whole speech profile.

25
00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:22.760
Predictable patterns, stable productions, and intact prosody support a functional explanation.

26
00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:30.040
Inconsistency, complexity breakdown, disrupted transitions, and unusual stress increase concern for apraxia.

27
00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:33.440
Combine formal articulation testing, connected speech, and

28
00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:35.620
a motor speech assessment when indicated.

29
00:01:35.660 --> 00:01:37.480
The conditions can coexist.

30
00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:40.660
Before labeling a disorder, also ask whether the productions

31
00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:44.030
are expected in the child's languages or dialects.
